  "reason": "For a d3 ion in an octahedral field, the 4T2g term has an energy of 10Dq. The 4T1g term rises more steeply, while the lowest doublets (2Eg and 2T1g) are nearly independent of field strength. At low Dq/B, the spin-allowed 4T2g and 4T1g terms are lowest; as Dq/B increases, the spin-forbidden 2Eg and 2T1g states become the lowest excited states."
